<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="glycerol-3-phosphate shuttle" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-6118" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: This pathway is on the list of Accept-If-Predicted Pathways (AIPP) generated for the COMET project, which includes pathways that are present widely throughout the plant kingdom. The AIPP list contains pathways that are automatically accepted if they are predicted for any plant species database. However, AIPP pathways are not automatically imported into databases if they are not predicted by the Pathologic program. &lt;A href=&quot;https://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; The rates of oxidation and reduction of NAD and NADH must be balanced for the continuation of both catabolism and anabolism. NADH, produced in the cytosol during glycolysis, need to be oxidized to NAD+. The net NADH oxidation process in the cell occurs primarily via mitochondrial respiration. However, NADH cannot traverse the inner mitochondrial membrane |CITS: [16661409]|. Therefore, cytosolic reducing equivalents must be transferred to the mitochondria through metabolite shuttles that operate between the two compartments. One such shuttle is the |FRAME: PWY-6118| (G3P shuttle). This shuttle involves the combined actions of a |FRAME: CPLX-7723| (EC 1.1.1.8) and a FAD-dependent |FRAME: CPLX-7724| (EC 1.1.5.3). The cytosolic enzyme consumes NADH during the conversion of |FRAME: DIHYDROXY-ACETONE-PHOSPHATE| to |FRAME: GLYCEROL-3P|, which can pass through the permeable mitochondrial outer membrane. |FRAME: GLYCEROL-3P| is then reoxidized to |FRAME: DIHYDROXY-ACETONE-PHOSPHATE| at the outer surface of the inner mitochondrial membrane by the mitochondrial FAD-dependent enzyme, which donates the electrons to the mitochondrial quinone pool. The |FRAME: DIHYDROXY-ACETONE-PHOSPHATE| is subsequently channeled back to the cytosol. The shuttle operates in yeast |CITS: [9171333][9559543]|, animals and plants |CITS: [16415206]|.</Description>
